<title>GERMANY: Ciampi did not meet Waigel on Sunday - sources.</title>
<headline>Ciampi did not meet Waigel on Sunday - sources.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-11-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italy's Treasury Minister Carlo Azeglio Ciampi did not meet German Finance Minister Theo Waigel on Sunday on his way to an emergency meeting of EU finance ministers in Brussels, German government sources said.</p>
<p>Italy's ANSA news agency had reported earlier on Sunday that Ciampi stopped over in Germany to meet Waigel. The German finance minister is not at the Brussels meeting.</p>
<p>&quot;He definitely did not meet Ciampi,&quot; a German government source said.</p>
<p>Europe's top financial policy-makers had to be called in after the EU's monetary committee of central bank and finance ministry officials failed on Saturday to agree a central parity rate for the lira's return to the EU's exchange rate mechanism (ERM).</p>
</text>
